#!/usr/bin/env python3
# route — pick the live seat for a task class, and keep the routing state honest.
#
# Contract C4 of docs/router-program.md. Stdlib only, same style family as
# clients/opus-runtime-doctor and clients/codex-routing-guard.
#
# Commands:
#   route pools  [--json]                        pool headroom (C1, or an accounts approximation)
#   route pick   <class> [--author-vendor V]     first routable chain entry for a class
#   route doctor [--write]                       probe seats and pools; write routing-state.json
#   route report [--days N]                      dispatch ledger joined with LB session cost
#   route learn  [--apply]                       propose (or write) chain demotions from outcomes
#
# Env:
#   AGENT_LB_URL       LB base URL (default http://127.0.0.1:2455)
#   ROUTE_TABLE        routing table path (default ~/.agent-lb/managed/coding-agents/routing-table.json,
#                      falling back to config/coding-agents/routing-table.json beside this script)
#   ROUTE_STATE        routing state path (default ~/.claude/routing-state.json)
#   ROUTE_ALERT        alert path (default ~/.claude/routing-ALERT)
#   ROUTE_LEDGER       dispatch ledger path (default ~/.claude/logs/dispatch.jsonl)
#   ROUTE_CURSOR_CMD   cursor probe command (default "cursor-agent status")
#   ROUTE_CODEX_CMD    codex probe command (default "node <codex-companion.mjs> status")
#   ROUTE_FIXTURE_DIR  TEST ONLY — serve HTTP reads from files in this directory instead of the
#                      network. A request to /api/pools reads api_pools.json; a missing file is a
#                      404. Never set this outside tests.
#
# Exit codes:
#   0  success
#   1  degraded (doctor: a probe failed) or operational failure
#   2  nothing routable / usage error

